  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes the outcomes and their probabilities, with an emphasis on treating outcome differences as negligible and choosing based on the probability of a favorable outcome. The individual similarly treats the outcome difference as insufficient to justify risk and emphasizes the 20% chance of nothing (i.e., disvalues the lower probability of a positive outcome in A). The individual’s reasoning aligns with preferring a higher chance of a positive result, even if smaller, over a riskier but potentially larger reward. This matches the rule of the decision reason: treat outcome differences as negligible and prefer the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. The verbal report reflects this logic clearly, indicating that the reason was used in the decision process.",
